oved","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:8ead28ed245bbf469a3c306c16aeda02f1cf3f807a801c192dca1d9fe5262af5","file":"preprints/A-radial-continuum-phase-transition-with-algebraic-decay-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":32,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"b025f1f914fe01d174dc05ce8886e6e009fc6f663e7fcaa6fe6e0f798094725f","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-radial-continuum-phase-transition-with-algebraic-decay-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:8ead28ed245bbf469a3c306c16aeda02f1cf3f807a801c192dca1d9fe5262af5","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-radial-continuum-phase-transition-with-algebraic-decay-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L32"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a bounded continuous function\n\\(\\phi:[0,\\infty)\\to\\R\\) and finite constants \\(B,C>0\\) such that\n\\[\n \\sum_{i<j}\\phi(\\abs{x_i-x_j})\\ge-BN,\n \\qquad\n \\abs{\\phi(r)}\\le C r^{-3-1/32}\\quad(r\\ge1).\n\\]\nThere are an open interval \\(I\\subset(0,\\infty)\\) centered at \\(5p/3\\)\nand a common inverse temperature \\(\\beta_c\\in[7/8,9/8]\\) such that,\nfor every \\(\\rho\\in I\\), the canonical free energy\n\\[\n f(\\beta,\\rho)=\n -\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}\\frac1{\\beta L^3}\n       \\log Z^\\phi_{L,\\lfloor\\rho L^3\\rfloor}(\\beta)\n\\]\nexists and is finite for every \\(\\beta>0\\).\nIts finite one-sided derivatives at \\(\\beta_c\\) satisfy\n\\[\n f'_-(\\beta_c,\\rho)>f'_+(\\beta_c,\\rho).\n\\]\nIn particular, \\(f(\\,\\cdot\\,,\\rho)\\) is not differentiable at \\(\\beta_c\\)."}
